A||||7||kornholio||Help, popping noise after changing spark plugs
Z||000000||kornholio||09-04-99||02:53 PM||||After I changed my spark plugs on my 86 SE, there is a popping noise about every 5-10 seconds.  Does anyone know what the cause is? I may have mixed up the right and the middle wires on the firewall side...would that cause a popping noise?  If I reverse them, will it cause any damage?  Thanks.
Z||000001||kornholio||09-04-99||03:00 PM||||Nevermind.  All is good now...Stupid me, I really did mix up the wires on the firewall side.  After checking my Haynes manual, I found that plug 2 and plug 4 were switched.
Z||000002||Dale||09-04-99||09:04 PM||||OUCH!!!
Z||000003||Bruce||09-05-99||11:16 AM||||I was nervous about the same thing, since you're working blind on that side. Luckily, I put all the wires back correctly.<br>Anyone find any rust on the upper portion of the old spark plugs. I think it was due to leaks in the rear lid, but I put gasket sealer in the spoiler bolt area, and that seems to help.<br>Is it wise to apply something on the threads to make the installation a little easier and prevent damage?
Z||000004||kornholio||09-05-99||11:32 AM||||Yeah, there was rust on the plugs on the firewall side.  The plugs on the firewall side weren't as hard to get to as I thought. All you need is an extention.  I was wondering if I should change my wires.  What difference will it make if I do?  More HP?
Z||000005||kornholio||09-05-99||11:35 AM||||Oh yeah, I also changed my air filter at the same time and I noticed that my acceleration was better.  Is that from the new plugs being put in, or is it the air filter?  The filter is a Canadian Tire brand.
Z||000006||Bruce||09-05-99||12:23 PM||||I think it's a good idea  to change the wires periodically because of the engine compartment heat. Next time, I'm going to install the protective spark plug boots to add a little more protection against water and heat.
Z||000007||Dale||09-05-99||04:13 PM||||Kornholio,<br>Its probably from both.  check out all the responces from your previous thread "spark plug questions" that should answer your questions on wires etc.
